    "paper_sentence": "the largest figure ratio, a measured error divided by the published figure, is 0.629 on the double lane and 0.819 on the single (main.tex sec:composition; supplement S12 panel A)",
    "double_lane_max_over_the_four_configurations": 0.629268025193091,
    "single_lane_max_over_the_four_configurations": 0.8191245254432976,
    "reproduces": true,
    "qualification": "0.629 is attained only on the fused route; the separate route's double-lane maximum is 0.6270981920683498. 0.819 is attained on both routes. The quoted pair is true as a maximum over the four configurations, but the sentence does not say that it is a maximum over them or name the route that attains the double-lane value; a reader can take 0.629 as a per-route figure, and the separate route does not attain it (its value is lower, so every cell is still inside the figure)."
